## Podman / Quadlets

Persistent services use Quadlet `.container` files.

```bash
# User services (rootless)
~/.config/containers/systemd/<name>.container
systemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user start <name>

# System services (rootful, requires sudo)
/etc/containers/systemd/<name>.container
systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl start <name>
```

Always include `Restart=on-failure` and SELinux volume labels (`:Z` single-use, `:z` shared).

---

## Environment Rules

- **Packages:** `dnf` only. `sudo` required for system installs. Log in `~/DEVBOX_INSTALLED.md`.
- **Containers:** Podman only. Never `docker` or `docker-compose`.
- **SELinux:** Always enforcing. Never `setenforce 0`.
- **Sessions:** Use `tmux` for anything over a minute.

## System Upgrade

```bash
sudo bootc upgrade && sudo reboot
# Rollback: sudo bootc rollback && sudo reboot
```

## Security

Hook suite active at `~/.claude/hooks/`. Sensitive paths blocked.
See `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (full context doc) for complete security model.
